    "note": "Both initial tests failed on both backends because of test assumptions: the naturally short font form did not fully hide its first editor at maximum offset, and the original UI resets to top on theme changes. A deterministic spacer between font rows now establishes offscreen/reveal coverage; dark/light checks require the observed native reset behavior while preserving the search query. Production viewport behavior did not change for these test corrections."
  },
  "contracts": [
    "Preference viewport extent, authoritative offset, clamp/reveal policy and allocation use the previously checked Rust model. The preferences shell no longer owns ScrollView synchronization/subscription state. Filter/category reset remains an explicit ScrollTo(0).",
    "The viewport interface now accepts theme background updates. The custom host and content layer receive the supplied color; opaque contents are marked opaque. The native baseline keeps ScrollView background handling and its original paint path without an extra Metal observer.",
    "New shared cases cover host ownership, wrapped font-form overflow/reveal, no-result collapse and reset, compact/wide resize, wheel/AX commands, dark/light reset with retained query, and profile-specific field values. Existing preference editor/IME, selector/action/switch capture and scene clipping cases retain their assertions through the common interface.",
    "No browser-service, store, profile/global scope, managed-setting validation, command/context admission or persistence policy changed. No dependency was added."
  ],
